<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
      xmlns:metal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/metal"
      xmlns:tal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/tal"
      metal:use-macro="here/main_template/macros/master"
>
  <body>
    <metal:content fill-slot="content">
      <h1>Release legacy page preview images</h1>

      <div class="portalMessage info"
           tal:condition="view/feedback"
      >
        <strong>Cleanup finished.</strong>
        <ul>
          <li tal:content="string:Objects processed: ${view/feedback/processed}">processed</li>
          <li tal:content="string:Objects cleaned: ${view/feedback/purged_objects}">cleaned</li>
          <li tal:content="string:Preview images released: ${view/feedback/purged_images}">released</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
      The blob files of the released images are removed by the next ZEO
      pack. Until the pack has run, no disk space is freed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
    Reviews now render their preview directly from the review PDF with
    pdf.js. The generated per-page preview images (pagePictures) are no
    longer created, and the copies stored on existing reviews are dead
    weight. This view deletes them from every review that has a usable
    PDF (uploaded or generated). Reviews without a PDF keep their images
    as their only visual and are listed below.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>This view cleans up the portal it is called on only.</strong>
    It must be run on all three portals:
        <code>/recensio</code>,
        <code>/regio</code>
         and
        <code>/altertum</code>. After all three runs, a ZEO pack is required
    to reclaim the disk space.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
      Objects with preview images and a PDF (will be cleaned):
          <strong tal:content="view/stats/cleanable_objects">0</strong>
      (preview images:
          <span tal:content="view/stats/cleanable_images">0</span>)
        </li>
        <li>
      Objects with preview images but no PDF (will be kept):
          <strong tal:content="python:len(view.stats['kept_urls'])">0</strong>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <details>
        <summary>Show the objects that keep their preview images</summary>
        <ul>
          <li tal:repeat="url view/stats/kept_urls">
            <a tal:content="url"
               tal:attributes="
                 href url;
               "
            >url</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </details>

      <form method="post"
            tal:condition="python:view.stats['cleanable_objects'] > 0"
      >
        <input name="_authenticator"
               type="hidden"
               tal:attributes="
                 value view/token;
               "
        />
        <input name="confirm"
               type="hidden"
               value="yes"
        />
        <button class="btn btn-danger"
                type="submit"
        >
      Release preview images now
        </button>
        <p>
      The cleanup runs inside this request and commits every 1000
      objects; on the large portal it can take a few minutes. Progress is
      written to the instance log.
        </p>
      </form>
    </metal:content>
  </body>
</html>
